1 NOTE {geni:about_me} * https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Per_Otto_Adelborg
2 CONT * http://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Adelborg_nr_2090
2 CONT * http://www.nad.riksarkivet.se/sbl/Presentation.aspx?id=5520
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Viaporin seurakunnan arkisto - I Aa:2 Rippikirja, Leskikuningattaren henkivartiorykmentti 1798-1808, jakso 37: Adelborg, Schultz?, Krämer, Boij, Blomm; Kansallisarkisto: https://astia.narc.fi/uusiastia/viewer/?fileId=6637880980&ai
2 CONC neistoId=1290331874 / Viitattu 22.9.2025
2 CONT
2 CONT Borgå, från Sveaborg 1801; Porvoon ruotsalaisen tuomiokirkkoseurakunnan arkisto - Seurakunnista saapuneet muuttokirjat 1799-1801, jakso 344: Petter Otto Adelborg; Kansallisarkisto: http://digi.narc.fi/digi/view.ka?kuid=7973254 
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
2 CONT Extra second lieutenant in the Dowager Queen's Life Regiment 1796-05-23 and second lieutenant with sergeant's salary 1798-04-14. Artillery and fortification exam 1798-07-12. Cornet in the Nyland Light Dragoon Corps 1801-06-16. Lie
2 CONC utenant in the army 1802-06-28. First Lieutenant 1805-05-04. Cavalry Commander of the Nyland Brigade's Light Dragoon Corps 1808-10-10. Cavalry Commander of the Life Regiment Brigade's Cuirassier Corps 1810-06-19. 2. Major of the L
2 CONC ife Grenadier Regiment's Armour Distribution 1811-12-23. RSO (KrAB.) 1814-08-10. Lieutenant Colonel in the Army 1814-05-22. 1st Major at Life Grenadier Regiment and distribution 1816-05-28. Dismissed 1818-02-03. (EÄ Lieutenant Col
2 CONC onel). Died 1818-03-02 in Västervik. He attended the war in Finland in 1808 with distinction (received a gold medal for bravery in the field in 1808) and, as chief of staff and chief adjutant under Major General Mörner, the Norweg
2 CONC ian campaign of 1814. He is known as an eminent caricaturist [Bbl]. See Biografica and the Swedish Biographical Dictionary. Married 1807-05-26 at Espoo Manor with Lovisa Eleonora Ramsay (from nr 215 Noble family)
2 CONT
2 CONT Riddare av Kungliga Svärdsorden 1814
