2 CONT Hans far Anders skal ha byggt ett stort hus på västerlånggatan  som senare skall ha kallats  Scharenbergska. (1750)
2 CONT
2 CONT Anders' son Lars inherited half of one of his father's houses and let his brother-in-law have it. The house stood at what today is Järntorget 83B.[5]
2 CONT
