1 NOTE {geni:about_me} From his wife Anna's death record: "On 6 April 1725, she married Mr. Peter Bursell, the appointed assessor and secretary of the province here in Umeå. She had only one son with him during their 29 years of marriage
2 CONC  [Anna married Bursell in 1725, and he died in 1757. That makes it 32 years, not 29!], who died in his prime, not long after his father. The father died on 11 December 1757 and the son on 26 February 1758."
2 CONT
2 CONT Sources:
2 CONT Marriage record to Anna Bröms, Maria Magdalena (AB) EI:1.292, 1725-04-06 (1706-1729) (AID: v88260.b150.s293, NAD: SE/SSA/0012), https://www.arkivdigital.se/aid/show/v88260.b150.s293
