2 CONT '''TABLE 1'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Lars Olofsson .''' 'Must have been descended from good old nobility, who in the coat of arms carried a laurel tree in a red field'. Bailiff over the k. the estate in Östergötland 1578, in Hammarkind 1578–1587, in Memming 1588–1
2 CONC 590 and again in Hammarkind 1598–1599. Castle bailiff at Stegeborg Castle. Died 1606-02-13 and is buried with his wife in Söderköping. '''Married to Helena Johansdotter , died 1608-02-16.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Laurentius Laurentii Laurinus senior ,''' born 1577 in Söderköping. Student in Uppsala 1594. Mag. in Wittenberg 19-10-1602. Vice rector at Söderköping's school in 1603. Rector scholae first. 11/15/1604. Parish priest in Härad
2 CONC shammar and Jonsberg parish of Linköping diocese 1609. Provost 1620. Died blind 11/22/1656. 'He was a good Latin poet and has published several writings from the press, including a chronicle of the kings of Sweden, everything from
2 CONC  Magog. His portrait can be found in Häradshammar's church's sacristy. '''Married 1st in 1605 to Margareta Larsdotter in her 2nd marriage (married 1st to the dean of Linköping Johannes Canuti Trelogius, born 1559 in Ringarum recto
2 CONC ry, Ög., died 1603 in the plague)''' 1 , born 1570, died 1620-07 -22, daughter of King Johan's commanding officer in several Eastern Goths fiefs, then the quartermaster in Öster- and Västergötland as well as Småland, Lars Joensson
2 CONC  and Kerstin Jakobsdotter. '''Married 2nd 1621-06-24 to Elisabet Ungia , died 1651-07-07, daughter of the superintendent in Kalmar, mag. Johannes Ungius and his 1st wife Helena Månsdotter.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1. '''Johan Larsson Laurinus ,''' born 1609. Councillor. Died 1686. born 1609-06-01. Student in Uppsala 1630-09-09. Disp. pp. Oh. Auditor 1634. Law reader in 12 districts in Uppland 1637. Healthcare clerk in Stockholm 2 1640-08-
2 CONC 18. Notary in the City Commissioner's Court 2 1648-05-12. City notary 1652. Councilor 1655. Resigned due to age and illness 1678. Died 1686-05-09 in Stockholm and buried p. Oh. 20/6 in Mary's church. 2 . '''Married 1:o 1640 to Eme
2 CONC rentia Roches ,''' buried 1655-08-10 in Maria church 2, daughter of the councilor and merchant in Gothenburg Paul Roches d. eh. '''Married 2nd 1656-01-01 in Stockholm Nikolai fors. in Stockholm 2 with Margareta Johansdotter Utter 
2 CONC , died 1710.'''
2 CONT * 1. '''Laurentius Laurentii Laurinus junior ,''' born 1613. Provost. Died 1672. born 1613-08-27 in Häradshammar rectory. Student in Uppsala 1631-03-06. Stomach. in Wittenberg in 1639, after which he continued his travels abroad a
2 CONC nd became poëta laureatus cæsareus and returned home in 1641. Eloquentiae and poëseos lecturer at Linköping's high school in 1642. Ordained priest 22-08-1643. Logices lector 1644. Historiarum and moralium lector 1650. First theolo
2 CONC gy lector and vicar in Skeda pastorate 1657. Also poenitenarius publicus 1656. Vicar in Söderköping 1659-08-03. Contract provost s. Oh. Died 1672-11-20 during the Riksdag in Stockholm [Hm]. '''Married 1641-06-19 to his stepmother'
2 CONC s niece Helena Wallerius ,''' born 1620, buried 1695-10-27, daughter of the dean and vicar in Högsby pastorate of Kalmar diocese Lars Wallerius and Catharina Ungia.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Christophorus Laurinus ,''' born 1642. Provost and vicar. Died 1702. born 1642-06-30 in Linköping. Student in Uppsala 1665-10-03. Stomach. 16-12-1679. Rector in Söderköping 1682. Parish priest in Törnevalla pastorate of Linkö
2 CONC ping diocese 1691. Contract priest s. Oh. Preses at the clergy meeting 1699. Died 1702 [Hm]. '''Married 1st in 1679 to Maria Widman ,''' died 1694-07-15, daughter of the vicar in Alsike pastorate of Uppsala archdiocese Johannes Wi
2 CONC dman and Lisbet Laurin. '''Married 2nd in 1696 to Margareta Sondel in her 1st marriage (married 2nd to the contract provost and vicar of the Husby-Sjutolft pastorate of the Uppsala archdiocese Anders Jäger in his 1st marriage, die
2 CONC d 1730), born 1672-03-10 , died in 1712, daughter of the vicar in Håtuna pastorate of the said diocese Nils Sundelius and Christina Johansdotter Achrælius [Hm].'''
2 CONT * '''Johan Laurin,''' ennobled Laurin , born 1643. Colonel. Died 1698. Kålstad in Risinge parish Östergötland county. Born 1643-04-26 (1645-04-21 according to the main banner in Risinge church). Enlisted as a soldier in the regime
2 CONC nt of the Governor of Brüssel Duc de Wilhermosa in 1661. Dismissed from there in 1662 and went as a lieutenant to the East Indies, where he served for three years. Returned to Sweden in 1668. Lieutenant of the Admiralty in 1670. T
2 CONC hen boatswain and finally captain, both at sea and on land, in Dutch service. Dismissal from the Dutch service at the outbreak of war between Sweden and Holland. Captain in Colonel John Mel's regiment at Karlsburg. Commandant at G
2 CONC ullberg redoubt 1676. Major in Prince Carl's life regiment 02-05-1677. Commandant at Ny-Älvsborg p. Oh. Ennobled 1678-02-23 (introd. 1680 under no. 926). Commandant at Hedvigsholm's redoubt at Marstrand 1679-10-29. Major at the Sw
2 CONC edish life regiment to foot 3 1680-06-01. Lieutenant colonel, at the Västgötadal regiment 1691-12-27. Colonel and commandant at Marstrand 1693-12-31. Died 1698-01-01 in Kålstad and closed his own adl. ate as well as buried s. Oh. 
2 CONC 3/7 in Risinge church, where his arms were set up. '''Married 1st to a Dutch woman. Married 2nd before 1679-11-25 to Ingeborg Roches , died 1705 at Kålstad and buried p. Oh. 7/6 in Risinge church, daughter of the councilor in Goth
2 CONC enburg Paul Roches and Marina NN.'''
