1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Laurentius Laurentii Laurinus, Sr.=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Lasse Olofsson and Helena Johansdotter
2 CONT * He is represented, among other things, in The Swedish Psalm Book 1986 with the text of the well-known hymn I himmelen, i himmelen (no. 169) which was published by Laurinus in connection with his wife's "funeral sermon" before th
2 CONC e departure from home. The hymn is included in Rune Lindström's film Himlaspelet from 1942, which is based on his play Ett spel om en väg som til Himla bir .
2 CONT * In addition to Psalms, he also wrote a series of theological works, and translated others from the Latin. Has also written a number of other writings, including En kort Sveriges chrönika from Magog alt inn til Fröken Christinas 
2 CONC regemente (1647) and a translation of Matthias Hafenreffer's theological compendium in 1650. 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.wikipedia.org/wiki/Laurentius_Laurinus Laurentius Laurinus, Swedish Priest and Writer, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Laurentius Laurentii Laurinus the elder, born 1573 or 1577 in Söderköping , died 29 November 1655 or 22 November (November 29) 1656 in Häradshammar parish . He was rector in Söderköping and parish priest in Häradshammar's parish i
2 CONC n Östergötland . In 1622 he published a music textbook, Musicae rudimenta pro incipientibus necessaria .
2 CONT
2 CONT Laurentius Laurinus the Elder was born in 1577 in Söderköping . He was the son of the castle bailiff at Stegeborg Lars Olofsson and Helena Johansdotter. Laurinus' father was from Scotland . Laurinus became a student at Uppsala Uni
2 CONC versity in 1594 and then studied abroad. He became a master in Wittenberg in 1603 and was ordained the same year. In 1603 Laurinus became vice-rector in Söderköping and in 1605 rector in Söderköping. In 1609 he became parish pries
2 CONC t in Häradshammar's parish and in 1620 contract provost in Vikboland's contract . Laurinus died blind on 29 November 1655 or 22 November (November 29) 1656 in Häradshammar's parish . [ 2 ]
2 CONT Laurinus was a Member of Parliament at the Riksdag in 1634 . [ 2 ] A portrait of Laurinus hangs in Häradshammar's church sacristy.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Family'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Laurinus married for the first time in 1605 to Margareta Larsdotter (1570–1620). She was the daughter of the commander of Vikbolandet Lasse Jonsson and Kjerstin Jacobsdotter. Margareta Larsdotter had previously been married to the
2 CONC  domprovost Johannes Canuti (Trelogius) in Linköping . Laurinus and Larsdotter together had the children Catharina Laurinus (1606–1607), the councilor Johannes Laurinus (1609–1686) in Stockholm , the vicar Laurentius Laurinus the 
2 CONC younger in St. Laurentii parish , Söderköping , as well as 6 daughters and 5 sons. [ 2 ] Laurinus married the second time on 24 June 1621 to Elisabeth Ungius (1602–1651). She was the daughter of the superintendent Johannes Petri U
2 CONC ngius and Helena Månsdotter in Kalmar
2 CONT
2 CONT =Links=
2 CONT
