1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Birth:''' 
2 CONT *  She is the sister of  Peter Dahlström, who came to Finland  as an accountant in  Kimo year 1703 and then after the war (1700-1721).   
2 CONT
2 CONT '''1st  Marriage:'''  Karl Feuchling / Füching  (1662-1697) 
2 CONT *  The daughter Anna was married to the regimental clerk Carl Feuchting (named in a protocol from 1707: the regimental clerk Olof Dahlström's former son-in-law, the late regimental clerk C.F.). The daughter's name was taken from a
2 CONC  note in the protocol dated July 12, 1704, where Olof Dahlström was asked : “Whether his daughter Anna Dahlström….. in relation to the farm of the blessed pastor Evert Feuchting (father-in-law)….. as far as the value and sale of t
2 CONC he farm is concerned”.
2 CONT *  Daughter  Margareta Feuchling.  
2 CONT
2 CONT '''2nd  Marriage about  1704 Petter Heicke:''' 
2 CONT * 1705 : p1234 Orisberg 	bruksförvalt. Petter Heicki, '''(wife:)''' hustru  Anna''',    http://suku.genealogia.fi/sukuwiki/index.php/Mantalsl%C3%A4ngd_Storkyro_Pro_1705 <br/>
2 CONT * Mantalbok 1708  p. 1487: ''' Bruksförwaltare Pett. Heike, hustru Anna Dahlström,'''  Pohjanmaan läänin tilejä - Tositekirja 1708 (9249b, f. 1171?2701), jakso 312, sivu 1487: Orisbergz Bruk; Kansallisarkisto: https://astia.narc.f
2 CONC i/uusiastia/viewer/?fileId=9573308956&aineistoId=1595462520 <br/>
2 CONT * Mantalbok 1709 p.1772:  Orisberg,''' bruksförv. Petter Heike, (wife:) hustru Anna Dahlström,''' br Anders Heike:   http://suku.genealogia.fi/sukuwiki/index.php/Mantalsl%C3%A4ngd_Storkyro_Pro_1709 <br/>
2 CONT * 1711:  Myös ensimmäisestä avioliitosta  syntynyt tytär Greta Feuchting  mainittu;  Pohjanmaan läänin tilejä - Tositekirja 1711 (9259, f. 1519-3127), jakso 209, sivu 1758; KA: : https://astia.narc.fi/uusiastia/viewer/?fileId=9851
2 CONC 465009&aineistoId=1596101322<br/>
2 CONT * 1713 Petter Heicke ja hustru,  Orisberg bruk.  Pohjanmaan läänin tilejä - Tositekirja 1713  (9267), jakso 1114, sivu 1122: Stookÿrå ; KA: https://astia.narc.fi/uusiastia/viewer/?fileId=9740509550&aineistoId=1596511206 <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT ''' Refugees in Sweden:''' 
2 CONT *  1714 Isokyrö and Orisberg  were ruined by russian soldiers. Peter Heicke  with his family in Sweden 1715-1716. Johanna Aminoff-Winberg: Finska flyktingar i Sverige under stora ofreden. Flyktingförteckningar. - Släktforskning rf
2 CONC :s publikationer 4(1995), 280 s. ISBN 951-96990-2-3. 1715 - 1716  as refugee in Sweden nr 3570, bruksförvaltare  Per Heike fr: Österbotten. barn: okänt antal. d: II. _med barn. https://www.genealogia.fi/hakem/flykting/flykting37.h
2 CONC tm ;  Flyktingkommissionen 1716 refugee  nr 4704 Petter Heike, bruksförwaltare , fr: Österbotten. b: okänt antal.    https://www.genealogia.fi/hakem/flykting/flykting38.htm <br/>
2 CONT
2 CONT '''About the Great Northern War:'''
2 CONT *  The Great Northern War (1700–1721) was a conflict involving Sweden, Russia, and other European powers. During this war, Russian troops advanced into Finland and Sweden’s Baltic provinces, leading to significant displacement of 
2 CONC people.
2 CONT *  Thousands of Swedish subjects fled from the advancing Russian forces. Initially, the Swedish royal power decreed that these refugees should cross the Baltic Sea and seek safety in Sweden. Between 20,000 and 30,000 refugees reac
2 CONC hed Sweden’s eastern coast during this period.
2 CONT *  Local Reception and Challenges: While central authorities formulated refugee reception policies, local communities played a crucial role in implementing them. Local authorities had to balance the refugees’ need for protection w
2 CONC ith their own demands for security.
2 CONT * Plague Outbreak and Its Impact: In September 1710, ships from Reval (Tallinn) carried the plague across the Gulf of Finland to Helsingfors (Helsinki) and Borgå (Porvoo). The plague devastated these areas, resulting in the loss o
2 CONC f lives among both inhabitants and refugees2. (Tietojen kokoamisessa avusti Copilot) 
