1 NOTE {geni:about_me} See the Profile PIC ''more clear in '''Media > Dovcuments'''.''
2 CONT
2 CONT NOT TO BE MIXED UP WITH: [https://www.geni.com/people/Claus-Friedrichsohn-Wilcken/6000000060265825311 '''Claes Wilcken'''], a son of Friedrich’s, who was born in Estonia. He was just a tradesman. He died in 1691. He was married to
2 CONC  Anna Rebelledi and got 15 children. She was married twice. She died in 1679. He was married twice. His heirs sold his grave in 1702, so they disgracefully dug him up.Claus Wilcken Friedrichson / Claes Willken Friederichsson / Cla
2 CONC es Wilchen Friderichs / Claes Wilken Fredrich / Claes Wilcken Fredericks, his name was spelled in many different ways, never with an s, was not in any way related to Claes Wilckens.
2 CONT
2 CONT Claes Wilckens(THIS PROFILE) was a very rich merchant and he married twice, to E von Bergen and E Speet,. He got 14 children from his first wife, and 3 children from his second wife. His second wife was married 3 times.
2 CONT
2 CONT Claes Wilckens died “bottomless rich”. His grave is intact. One of his buildings is still proudly standing in The Old Town of Stockholm.
2 CONT
2 CONT 1676 öfverläts förvaltningen af Abraham Momma-Reenstiernas västmanländska bruk (Färna)  och  åt stockholmsborgaren Claes Wilckens.
2 CONT
2 CONT Abraham Momma blev tvungen att pantförskriva Färna till Claes Wilkens, vars ättlingar och släkt drev bruket åren 1692-1789. År 1737 omnämns Färna som stålbruk med brännugn och plåthammare samt tre stångjärnshammare.
