1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Below is an account from Burke's of Anne Mary Macnamara's immediate family:  A genealogical and heraldic history of the landed ... www.ebooksread.com/.../page-59-a-genealogical-and-heraldic-history-of-the-landed-..
2 CONC .
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur Macnamara, of Llangoed Castle, Brecknockshire, son of John Macnamara, of Llangoed Castle (by Mary his wife, dau. and heir of Arthur Jones, Esq. of Llangoed Castle), Col. Westminster Regt. of Middlesex Militia, and M.P., m. 
2 CONC Anne, dau. of William Lee, Esq., and heir of John Pedley, Esq. of Caddington Hall, and by her (who d. 3 May, 1870) had issue,
2 CONT
2 CONT Arthur, now of Caddington Hall, Herts, and Billington Manor House, Beds, J.P. and D.L., County Councillor, late Capt. Beds Militia, b. 23 Sept. 1829 ; m. 28 Sept. 1854, Lady Sophia Eliza Hare, 3rd dau. of William, 2nd Earl of List
2 CONC owel, J.P.
2 CONT
2 CONT John, twin with Arthur, b. 1829; m. 12 April, 1860, Sarah, eldest dau. of Edward Naylor Vickers, Esq. of Tapton Hall, Sheffield, and has Arthur, who d., and two daughters.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne Mary, m. Baron Adelsward, late Minister of Sweden in Paris.
2 CONT
2 CONT Elizabeth, m. Viscount Ernest de Rotalier, of Chateau de Rotalier, pres Beaufort, departement du Jura, France.
